    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "A monk asked Daishu Ekai, What is nirvana?",
      "path": "audio/1971-353/02.mp3",
      "start": 1.736735,
      "end": 4.70805
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "The master answered: Not to commit oneself to the vicious circle of birth and death or pleasure and pain is great nirvana.",
      "path": "audio/1971-353/03.mp3",
      "start": 6.0047619999999995,
      "end": 12.828254
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "What then is the vicious circle of birth and death and pleasure and pain?",
      "path": "audio/1971-353/04.mp3",
      "start": 14.094898,
      "end": 17.710385000000002
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "The master said: To desire nirvana!",
      "path": "audio/1971-353/05.mp3",
      "start": 19.020045,
      "end": 22.338685
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "Now be silent and feel what is meant by to desire nirvana, and remember that I am not saying think about it because to think is to miss it.",
      "path": "audio/1971-353/06.mp3",
      "start": 23.824966,
      "end": 32.946349
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "Feel it.",
      "path": "audio/1971-353/07.mp3",
      "start": 34.34805,
      "end": 35.197731999999995
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "Feel it.",
